  "facts": [
    "Gisund Bridge, a cantilever marvel, spans 1,147 metres across the Gisundet strait, its longest 143‑metre main span anchoring the road between mainland Finnsnes and island village Silsand.",
    "Opened on 23 June 1972, the bridge offers a 41‑metre clearance beneath, allowing sizable vessels to glide beneath its sturdy 25‑span structure.",
    "Constructed as part of Norwegian County Road 86, Gisund Bridge links the remote island of Senja to the mainland, transforming regional travel and commerce."
